/-!
# The keystone at a K-flat pair, with the monoidality comparison of [stacks 068I] in place

`Dualizing.tensorBaseChangeMor_eq_of_degreewise_unit` reduces the [stacks 068I] identification at a
pair of K-flat complexes to one equation between localized chain maps, whose [stacks 068I] side
carries the [stacks 0A63] uncurrying of a chain map `w` presenting the prefix, composed with the
chain-level map of [stacks 0E1W].  That uncurrying is not evaluated there:
`Stacks.DerivedHom.BaseChangeIso.uncurry_unit_comp_restrictScalars_map_comp_changeOfRingsMap`, the
chain-level mate square, evaluates it only at a morphism which is the degreewise unit of extension
of scalars followed by the restriction of a transpose, and `w` is an arbitrary chain map.

`Stacks.DerivedHom.BaseChangeIso.exists_uncurry_unit_value` removes that obstruction: `w` lands in
the restriction along the lifted ring map of a complex over the lift of `A`, so it *is* a
transpose, and the mate square applies to it.  This file substitutes the resulting value into the
keystone.

What that buys is the monoidality comparison.  The equation the keystone is reduced to here
carries `CochainComplex.ExtendScalars.extendScalarsMonoidalIso` at the pair of scalar lifts of `K`
and `L` -- the pair of *ordinary* complexes, which is the only pair at which the comparison of
[stacks 068I] is available -- together with the degreewise unit of extension of scalars at their
tensor product on the same side.  No lax monoidal structure map of restriction of scalars, and no
uncurrying of the prefix, occurs on either side.

So the remaining content of the [stacks 068I] identification at a K-flat pair is the comparison of
two monoidality isomorphisms: the one of the chosen model, which enters through the hypothesis
`_ha` pinning the prefix, and `CochainComplex.ExtendScalars.extendScalarsMonoidalIso` over the
lifted ring map, which the mate square has put on the [stacks 0GMT] side.

**What is not done here.**  Nothing is registered and no caveat is lifted.  Both hypotheses of
`Dualizing.tensorComparisonCompatibility_of_tensorBaseChangeMor` remain open; in particular the
comparison identity `h` is untouched, and its frontier remains
`Dualizing.tensorComparisonCompatibility_of_kFlat_tail`.  What this file changes is that the other
hypothesis, at a K-flat pair, no longer mentions the uncurrying of the prefix.

## Main results

* `Dualizing.tensorBaseChangeMor_eq_of_monoidal_chain_level` -- the [stacks 068I] identification at
  a pair of K-flat complexes, from one equation in which the [stacks 068I] prefix enters only
  through its transpose and the monoidality comparison of [stacks 068I] over the lifted ring map
  stands at the pair of scalar lifts.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A63](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A63)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 068I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/068I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E1W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E1W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GMT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GMT)
-/

@[expose] public section

